License history

Up to and including commit e673b26 (2026-10-24), Qython was published under
the Apache License, Version 2.0. Copies obtained under those terms keep them.
Every version after that commit is licensed under AGPL-3.0-only.

Why AGPL: anyone may use, study, modify and redistribute Qython, including
doctors and institutions running it for themselves. Whoever offers a modified
version to other people over a network must make the modified source available
to those users (AGPL section 13). That keeps improvements to clinical software
open instead of turning into closed copies.

