Third-party services and components

Qython can integrate with third-party services that are governed by their own
terms and are NOT covered by this license:

  - Google Gemini API (generative models, when the user supplies a key)
  - Groq API (speech-to-text fallback, optional)
  - Lastreo (medical credential verification, optional)
  - Google Drive API (optional backup of the user's own documents)
  - Firebase Authentication (optional)

Bundled and downloaded components keep their own licenses, among them
PyMuPDF (AGPL-3.0), and model weights downloaded at runtime
(faster-whisper large-v3-turbo, intfloat/multilingual-e5-base,
cross-encoder/mmarco-mMiniLMv2-L12-H384-v1, and local language models such as
Gemma or MedGemma), each under its upstream license.
